.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-INVITE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-invite - Invite a member by email, including before signup


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team invite <team> <email> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Invite a member by email, including before signup

.PP
Invite one exact account to the selected team at its current generation. The recipient must accept; an invitation is not immediate membership or a resource grant.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant machine use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for invite

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
